ch com department in the english  department  and so you know there's there's a lot of  things  in the world of philosophy that are  rather contingent  and what we study what we get introduced  to  is so contingent on who we encounter  and what they put in front of us so i  was so  fortunate that i had somebody  not my professors but somebody else who  could toss these books in my lap  and give me some other things to read  and work on  and fill in some of the gaps in my  understanding of  what you know what was interesting and  worth  studying at the time so i should say a  belated thanks to yoshihiro manoa  you know some of these books i've  returned to over and over again  in the course of my career and my  intellectual life  um we're talking about something that  that happened  you know decades ago and still has some  impact on me and on the videos that i i  shoot for  all of you someday down the line if i  had to pick one of these that i'd like  to get to  the first someday maybe i'll actually  shoot some stuff on problems of  dostoevsky's  poetics and on bhaktine himself i know  people would probably rather see uh  anti-oedipus and dialectic of  enlightenment and the order of things  but  you know you got to go where your heart  is i think and i  resonate more with bach team than i do  with these other  authors so you know we'll see what  happens in the future with these  interesting books that i was gifted  you

